Hi,

I am working on some decaying data with time (10 intervals). The 
response variable is a probability value, which I transform through the 
logit link function. I use a linear mixed model to capture the 
intercepts and the individual slopes for each subject based on time. The 
intercept and slope values are used for some other working analysis.

The problem I have is that AIC is large. I have checked other things 
such as plotting of transformed data, the fitted lines, their residuals 
etc.

Checking the distribution after logit transformation I find that the two 
extreme values (in original scale) almost 0 and almost 1 are quite 
frequent and they distort the results. So if we assume that the two 
extreme values are starting points and the ending points, (I have 
thousands of points for the whole data) by removing them the 
distribution of the transformed response is showing with a better shape. 
Again fitting one linear model through mixed model, it improves AIC by 
