Here are three responses I received when I asked the
same question last month. Sorry it took me this long
to post the summary. I would like to thank
Tim Hesterberg, Spencer Graves and Jo Jiao.
for their help. I think Jo's suggestion is
for elementwise power (rather than matrix power).

Regards,

Joseph Beyene 

******** Response-1 **************************

Try this

power.matrix <- function(M, n){
  #Raise matrix M to the n'th power
        powers <- base(n, 2)
        result <- diag( nrow(M) )
        for(i in 1:length(powers)) {
                if(powers[i])
                        result <- result %*% M
                M <- M %*% M
        }
        result
}

base _ function(m, b){
  #Express m as powers of b; m may be vector
  maxi <- floor(log(max(m))/log(b))
  result <- matrix( 0, length(m), maxi+1 )
  for(i in 1:(maxi+1)) {
    result[,i] _ m %% b
    m _ m %/% b
  }
  result
}

Tim Hesterberg
