From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Fri Jul  4 06:51:48 2003
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Fri, 04 Jul 2003 07:51:48 +0100
Subject: Re: lm inside apply ?
In-Reply-To: <C497480353EF904FBF7A8B0851E5422C9F7B36@MAIL002.AD.MLP.COM>
References: <C497480353EF904FBF7A8B0851E5422C9F7B36@MAIL002.AD.MLP.COM>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0307040744430.3588-100000@gannet.stats>

Use coef(lm(stockret ~ markret))[, 2] to do the 100 fits and extract the
coefficients.

Using apply will not avoid looping, just do it internally, and it would 
wastefully repeat a lot of computations.  But you could use something like

apply(stockret, 1, function(x) coef(lm(x ~ market))[2])

if you want to understand how to do it.

If my first suggestion had not been available you could go back to your 
textbooks and program the b = S_xy/S_xx formula using matrix operations.

