Subject: Re: ANOVA on repeated measures with missing data
Message-ID: <E09E527B56BE2D438A3D6A246DDD27A9165DC7@roper-cv.qld.cmis.CSIRO.AU>

When there are no missing values I presume the design is then orthogonal, in
which case you will have information on each separate effect in one stratum
only.  (This is the goal of most split-plot designs, which you have).

When there are missing values the design is no longer orthogonal and you
have information on some effects both from within and between Id
comparisons.  I would recommend you try lme() for such non-orthogonal cases,
by the way, as it automatically recovers 'inter- and intra-block'
information and packages the result in possibly a less puzzling way.

bill Venables.

