These are just triangular numbers (do a google search for some 
fun).  If there's no other reason to do it in a loop, 
cumsum(0:45) should do it (if you know at which n to stop).  If you just know the upper limit (say 1000 roughly), then solve the
equation 

 

    1000 =
(n+1)*n/2

 

which can be done by ceiling(uniroot(function(x) 
0.5*x*(x+1)-1000, c(1, 100))$root), if you don't remember the root of
quadratic 
equations.

 

Andy

