From phlasky at earthlink.net  Fri Jul 11 16:19:35 2003
From: phlasky at earthlink.net (Paul H. Lasky)
Date: Fri, 11 Jul 2003 09:19:35 -0700
Subject: Replace apply with colMeans, etc
Message-ID: <001401c347c8$38761580$69aeb2d1@ELNphlasky>

    In building a simulation 
program in S-Plus 6.1, windows, I must calculate some column 
means of a matrix (NOT a data frame)  (many times) x 10 ^ 
5.  I was surprised to find that the function colMeans is about 80% faster 
than  calculating the means with apply !  E.g.

 

 test = matrix(runif(4*18,1,100), 
ncol=4)
sys.time({for(i in 1:10000) colMeans(test)})
[1] 108.97 
108.97
> sys.time({for(i in 1:10000) apply(test,2,mean)})
[1] 180.1 
180.1

    Conclusion:  Replace 
the apply function with colMeans or colSums in all your scripts and AVOID using 
apply when you can use these newer functions.

 

  Paul H. Lasky

  P & B Consultants

  Rancho Santa Fe, CA

 

 

