> your scripts and AVOID using apply when you can use these newer functions.
>
>  Paul H. Lasky
>  P & B Consultants
>  Rancho Santa Fe, CA

If you want to go even faster, use `fastColMeans', which
is part of the resampling library.

> x _ diag(3) + 1.0
> sys.time(for(i in 1:1000) temp _ colMeans(x))
[1] 2.52 2.52
> sys.time(for(i in 1:1000) temp _ fastColMeans(x))
[1] 0.66 0.66
> sys.time(for(i in 1:1000) temp _ fastColMeans(x, 2)) # if you know the 
> dimension
[1] 0.46 0.46
(80% faster yet, though the gains will be less for larger matrices.)

The library also has some other goodies, e.g.
        anyMissing()
        notSorted()
which are substantially faster than the usual ways to check
these conditions.

For more info see www.insightful.com/Hesterberg/bootstrap

Also,
        www.insightful.com/Hesterberg/articles/EfficientSplus.txt
has tips on faster programming.

